  "raw_response": "```json\n{\n  \"modifications\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Introduce a fluorine atom at the C-14 position of the anthracycline core to enhance binding affinity to mutated Topoisomerase II.\",\n      \"smiles\": \"COc1cccc2C(=O)c3c(O)c4c(c(O)c3C(=O)c12)[C@@H](O[C@H]1C[C@@H](N)[C@H](O)[C@@H](C)O1)C[C@]4(O)C(=O)COF\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Fluorine atoms can enhance drug-target interactions through hydrophobic and electronic effects, potentially overcoming mutations that reduce binding.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Add a methoxy group to the C-3' position of the sugar moiety to improve steric compatibility with drug-resistant Topoisomerase II variants.\",\n      \"smiles\": \"COc1cccc2C(=O)c3c(O)c4c(c(O)c3C(=O)c12)[C@@H](O[C@H]1C[C@@H](N)[C@H](O[C@H](C)OC)[C@@H](C)O1)C[C@]4(O)C(=O)CO\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Introducing a methoxy group at the sugar moiety can help evade steric hindrance caused by mutations in the binding site.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Replace the C-10 hydroxyl group with an amino group to improve hydrogen bonding with mutated residues in Topoisomerase II.\",\n      \"smiles\": \"COc1cccc2C(=O)c3c(O)c4c(c(O)c3C(=O)c12)[C@@H](O[C@H]1C[C@@H](N)[C@H](N)[C@@H](C)O1)C[C@]4(O)C(=O)CO\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Amino groups can form stronger hydrogen bonds compared to hydroxyl groups, potentially compensating for resistance-associated binding changes.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
